Compatibility patch for upstream SPIDERMAN (Louden & Kreidberg 2018, https://github.com/tomlouden/spiderman), commit 379a5b6, so that it builds
and runs with numpy >= 2, matplotlib >= 3.3 and current setuptools. It changes no physics: the patched SPIDERMAN is the baseline of section 7 of
validation/speed_accuracy.ipynb. SPIDERMAN is under the GNU GPL v3, and so is this patch.

    git clone https://github.com/tomlouden/spiderman.git
    cd spiderman
    git checkout 379a5b6
    git apply /path/to/HyperPhase/validation/spiderman_numpy2.patch
    pip install .

The changes: NPY_IN_ARRAY -> NPY_ARRAY_IN_ARRAY in c_src/_web.c and c_src/_heron.c (the alias is gone from the numpy 2 headers); setup.py without
numpy.distutils (removed in numpy 2) and with the licence as a string, plus a pyproject.toml that builds against numpy >= 2; in spiderman/,
matplotlib.image.imread for the removed matplotlib._png.read_png (plot.py), an object array for the ragged grid (read_model.py), and a boolean
mask instead of a list holding one (stellar_grid.py).

